WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.469
-The White House is now
threatening to obstruct

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.737
the impeachment inquiry

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.439
and refusing to cooperate
with subpoenas.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.175
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.712
♪♪

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.480
As a candidate for president,

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.417
Trump echoed years of
empty Republican rhetoric

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.853
about the sanctity
of our Constitution

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.721
and claimed that he wanted
to restore the values enshrined

00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:25.325
by the founding fathers,
although, as always,

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.461
it was clear that he had no idea
what he was talking about.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:32.698
-It's all about the Constitution
of -- of --

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.333
And -- And so important.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:38.504
The Constitution
the way it was meant to be.

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.274
The mainstream media

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.177
wants to surrender
our Constitution.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.980
I feel very strongly
about our Constitution.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.414
I'm proud of it. I love it.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:50.483
And I want to go through
the Constitution --

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.951
That's what we want to do.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.286
I mean, we want to bring
the Constitution back.

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.822
-What -- What do you mean,
bring it back?

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:58.958
It didn't go anywhere.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.560
He talks about the Constitution

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.029
like it's a college student
who took a gap year

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.364
and now wants to stay
in Barcelona

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.332
because it met someone.

00:01:07.332 --> 00:01:08.768
"Come back, Constitution.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.804
Katarina is only
gonna break your heart."

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.607
Now, the impeachment inquiry
currently happening in the House

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.109
isn't just an investigation
of President Trump's

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.811
many corrupt abuses of power.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.380
It's also a test of our system
in which Congress

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.717
is supposed to be a co-equal
branch of the government.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.886
And yesterday,
the Trump administration

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.988
did its best
to undermine that system

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.023
by declaring itself
above the law.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.759
-President Trump continuing
to stonewall House Democrats

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.628
in their investigation efforts.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.897
The White House
sending a scathing letter

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.666
to House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
and House committees

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:44.337
refusing to cooperate,
calling the impeachment inquiry

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:47.039
illegitimate and
unconstitutional.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:49.309
-That's right. Trump is
literally calling impeachment,

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:52.778
a process which is laid out
in the Constitution,

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.280
unconstitutional.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.881
He's going to be so shocked

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:58.017
if he ever reads
the Constitution one day.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.385
"Let's see here.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:03.422
Oh, no! Oh, no!

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.191
Oh, boy!

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.759
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.261
High crimes AND misdemeanors?

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.030
I did both of those
this morning.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.367
Oh, there better not be anything
in here about golf. Oh, no!"

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.103
This idea that impeachment
is somehow unconstitutional

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.472
is an insane theory
that has been percolating

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.106
on the right
for a few weeks now.

00:02:21.106 --> 00:02:23.976
Over the weekend, for example,
a Fox News guest suggested

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.812
that Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.780
should actually change the rules

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.250
to, in his words,
protect the Constitution.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.553
-If I were the Senate
majority leader,

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:37.156
I'd tell the House,
"This is dead on arrival.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:40.626
We're changing the rules,
and we're not going to follow up

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:41.960
with an impeachment trial here.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.297
We're not required to
under the Constitution.

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:47.033
-But good ol' Mitch McConnell
is all, "Yeah, yeah, they do.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.168
We're gonna have to listen
to it. We'll have a trial."

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.437
I mean, what's up with that?!

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.372
-Well, that's --
Those are the current rules.

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:56.208
They could change the rules
to protect the Constitution.

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:58.077
-They literally want
to change the rules

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.345
because they're losing.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.914
It's like if the Jets
were down 45-0 at halftime

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.650
and said,
"We want to change the rules

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.420
to let running backs have SUVs."

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.057
Also, you really --
you really got to respect

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.392
Jeanine Pirro's
hard-hitting question there.

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.194
-What's up with that?!

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.662
-She's like --

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:20.232
She's like an angry Fox News
version of Jerry Seinfeld.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:23.069
[as Seinfeld] "You ever notice
how the Constitution

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:26.406
allows Congress to remove
a corrupt president?

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.373
What's the deal with that?!"

00:03:28.373 --> 00:03:30.176
[ "Seinfeld" bumper music
plays ]

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.645
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:37.917
Now, not only is this argument

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.286
a threat to the very foundations
of democracy,

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.655
it's also incredibly dumb,
which, of course, undercuts

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.158
the image Trump and his aides
love to project,

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.092
that he's some sort of
political mastermind

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:48.961
who's a genius
at manipulating the press.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.864
For example, here's what
one senior Trump official

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.133
had to say last week
about the President testing out

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.170
different arguments to defend
himself against impeachment.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:16.321
That, for real, sounds like
a sixth-grade prank designed

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:20.026
to get Trump to say the words
"I'm a master baker."

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.995
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:25.598
"Who? Me?
Are you guys talking about me?

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:31.004
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.
I'm a big-time master baker.

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.539
Sometimes twice in one day."

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.507
So, now Trump,
the monster baker,

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:38.544
has settled on a strategy
of basically declaring himself

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:41.347
above the Constitution,
and that's because Trump is

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.015
fundamentally
a thuggish authoritarian

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:44.683
who thinks he can do
whatever he wants

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:46.819
and even uses the language
of authoritarians

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.121
whenever he talks about
his powers as president,

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:52.425
whether it's declaring
a national emergency
to build a border wall

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:55.528
or asking foreign governments
to interfere in our elections.

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:09.808
-He told "The New York Times"
tonight...

00:05:09.808 --> 00:05:13.846
"I have the absolute right
to do what I want to do

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.781
with the Justice Department."

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:19.619
-I have the absolute right to
declare a national emergency.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:22.021
-I have an absolute right
to call national security.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.356
We need strong borders.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:26.258
-I do have an absolute right
to pardon myself.

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.794
-No, you do not have
the absolute right

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:29.928
to do whatever you want.

00:05:29.928 --> 00:05:31.898
Trump just likes
to say stuff like this

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:35.201
because he loves stroking his
ego to make himself feel better.

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.136
You know, he's a master baker.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:40.506
So, where exactly
does Trump think

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.308
he gets all these
magical powers from?

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.710
Well, he keeps saying article II
of the Constitution,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.679
which outlines
the powers of the presidency,

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:49.048
gives him license
to do whatever he wants.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.350
-Article II allows me
to do whatever I want.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.419
Then I have an Article II

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.954
where I have the right to do
whatever I want as president,

00:05:55.954 --> 00:05:58.924
but I don't even talk
about that.

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:01.260
-Nobody ever mentions
Article II.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.929
It gives me all of these rights

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:06.766
at a level that nobody
has ever seen before.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.600
We don't even talk
about Article II.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.169
-Okay.
First of all, that's wrong.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.437
Second, what do you mean,
no one ever talks about it?

00:06:12.437 --> 00:06:13.873
It's the Constitution.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:16.709
He talks about
our nation's founding document

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.577
like it's an underrated TV show.

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:21.547
"Nobody ever talks
about Schitt's Creek.

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:23.216
You guys got to see it.

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:25.484
It's got some of
Catherine O'Hara's best work."

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:29.755
Of course, we know that Trump
has never had even a hint

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.991
of intellectual curiosity
about what the Constitution

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:33.826
actually says when it comes

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.727
to the powers of the president
or Congress.

00:06:35.727 --> 00:06:38.064
In fact, one of his former
aides, Sam Nunberg,

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:40.599
once told a journalist
that it was his job

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:43.335
during the campaign to educate
Trump on the Constitution

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:44.837
but that he didn't get very far

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:46.806
before Trump stopped
paying attention.

00:06:54.813 --> 00:06:56.782
And I believe this story
because Trump always makes it

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:57.950
very obvious when he's bored.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.651
Just watch him
whenever he's in a meeting

00:06:59.651 --> 00:07:01.720
and someone else is speaking.
He looks straight down

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.189
and literally hugs himself
for comfort.

00:07:04.189 --> 00:07:06.158
"It's okay. It's okay.

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:09.294
Soon the bad man who's not you
will stop talking."

00:07:09.294 --> 00:07:10.663
In fact, you can see the result

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:12.431
of Trump's nonexistent
attention span

00:07:12.431 --> 00:07:14.366
when he tries to repeat
details of stories

00:07:14.366 --> 00:07:17.403
that got dumped into
the polluted river of his brain

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.037
and warped by all
that toxic sludge

00:07:19.037 --> 00:07:20.606
that's just sloshing around
in there --

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:23.375
like when he told a story on
Monday about a military briefing

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:25.578
that made absolutely
no sense whatsoever.

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:28.214
-When I took over our military,
we didn't have ammunition.

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:32.885
I was told by a top general,
maybe the top of them all.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:35.354
"Sir, I'm sorry, sir.
We don't have ammunition."

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:37.322
I said I'll never let
another president

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:40.425
have that happen to him or her.

00:07:40.425 --> 00:07:42.160
We didn't have ammunition.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.830
-Now, that was vaguely based
on something real.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.033
In early 2017, the military

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:49.334
reportedly was worried
about a shortage of bombs,

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:51.837
so sort of in the neighborhood
but not really close.

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:54.974
The story got warped so badly
in Trump's rotting brain

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:56.708
that it turned into
an incoherent rant

00:07:56.708 --> 00:07:59.946
about a top general,
maybe the top of them all,

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:03.282
coming to him and saying,
"We have no ammunition."

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.784
Like, first of all,
what do you mean

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:07.653
he was a top general,
maybe the top of them all?

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:10.322
He was either a top general
or he wasn't.

00:08:10.322 --> 00:08:12.758
In the military,
there's no gray area

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.694
about who's at the top.

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:16.228
You don't have to google it.

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:18.330
"Well, according to TripAdvisor,
he's number one,

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:21.733
but Yelp says
he's only three stars."

00:08:21.733 --> 00:08:23.936
Second, can we hear --

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.437
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:25.437 --> 00:08:28.107
Can we hear what this top
general supposedly said again?

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:31.110
-"Sir, I'm sorry, sir.
We don't have ammunition."

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.678
-That is not how generals talk.
He might have said, "Sir,

00:08:33.678 --> 00:08:35.981
we are currently experiencing
a shortage of ordinance."

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:37.583
But this dummy over here heard,

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.051
"Sir, we don't have
bullets, sir.

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:41.320
We've been throwing kitchen
supplies at the enemy, sir.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:44.089
We got one guy out there running
around with a food processor.

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:46.692
Sir, he hasn't killed anyone,

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.228
but he's becoming
a real master baker."

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:50.595
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.595 --> 00:08:52.698
So it's not a surprise --

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:55.835
It's not a surprise that this is
the same self-obsessed idiot

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:58.103
who thinks impeachment
is unconstitutional

00:08:58.103 --> 00:09:00.706
and insists he has the absolute
right to do whatever he wants.

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:02.407
And now he's
actively obstructing

00:09:02.407 --> 00:09:03.943
the impeachment inquiry.

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:05.411
For example, yesterday,

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:07.779
the White House blocked a key
player in the Ukraine scandal,

00:09:07.779 --> 00:09:10.383
an ambassador named Gordon
Sondland, from testifying.

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:12.784
Now, Sondland came
to prominence last week

00:09:12.784 --> 00:09:16.088
after a series of damning new
text messages was released

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:18.323
in which State Department
officials expressed concern

00:09:18.323 --> 00:09:20.293
to Sondland
about the quid pro quo

00:09:20.293 --> 00:09:21.894
Trump was dangling with Ukraine.

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:23.829
Sondland was one of
the key players

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:24.930
involved in that quid pro quo,

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.466
and at one point
during the text exchanges,

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:29.668
he realized
he should not be texting

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.170
about this scandal at all.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.440
-On September 1st, the top
U.S. diplomat in Ukraine,

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.309
Bill Taylor, texted the
U.S. ambassador to E.U.,

00:09:37.309 --> 00:09:39.912
Gordon Sondland,
and writes this.

00:09:48.887 --> 00:09:50.923
-Oh, man.
Any time you text someone

00:09:50.923 --> 00:09:53.859
and they write back, "Call me,"
it is not good.

00:09:53.859 --> 00:09:55.327
It's like if you texted
your fiancée,

00:09:55.327 --> 00:09:56.962
"Can't wait
to get married tonight,"

00:09:56.962 --> 00:09:58.731
and they just wrote back,
"Call me,"

00:09:58.731 --> 00:10:03.168
you'd better find out if that
honeymoon sweet is refundable.

00:10:03.168 --> 00:10:05.470
So, naturally, the Democrats
want to interview Sondland

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:07.039
as part of
the impeachment inquiry,

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.975
but Trump is simultaneously
blocking Sondland

00:10:08.975 --> 00:10:10.542
from testifying
while also claiming

00:10:10.542 --> 00:10:13.011
that he would love
to let Sondland testify.

00:10:13.011 --> 00:10:14.847
-On Twitter,
the President insisted

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:17.983
he would love to send
Ambassador Sondland to testify,

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:20.552
but, unfortunately,
he would be testifying

00:10:20.552 --> 00:10:23.588
before a totally compromised
kangaroo court.

00:10:23.588 --> 00:10:25.925
-I'm sorry. You're calling them
a kangaroo court?

00:10:25.925 --> 00:10:28.127
You're the one who literally
puffs out your chest

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:30.396
like you're defending
your territory.

00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:33.732
Fundamentally, what Trump's
behavior proves once again

00:10:33.732 --> 00:10:36.234
is that all those years
of empty Republican rhetoric

00:10:36.234 --> 00:10:38.637
about respecting the
Constitution were a fraud.

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:40.539
Republicans are falling in line
behind a guy

00:10:40.539 --> 00:10:42.541
who's declaring himself
above the Constitution

00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:45.344
and claiming absolute powers
to do whatever he wants.

00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:47.712
We've had corrupt, lawless
presidents before,

00:10:47.712 --> 00:10:49.115
but Trump is the top.

00:10:49.115 --> 00:10:51.082
-Maybe the top of them all.

00:10:51.082 --> 00:10:52.985
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:55.121
[ Cheers and applause ]

